# The Supabase config for `pnpm dev`.
#
# This was `.env.online`, loaded only by a second `dev:online` script, so the
# ordinary dev server could not play online at all - which read as a missing
# feature rather than a policy. There is one kind of game and the player picks
# local or online inside it, so there is one dev server.
#
# `development`, not a plain `.env`: a plain one is loaded in EVERY vite mode,
# `test` included, which would hand all the unit tests a network-enabled config.
# `onlineConfig.test.ts` asserts that has not happened.
#
# The e2e suite starts this same server, and its offline promise is now
# ENFORCED rather than assumed: playwright.config.ts blackholes the backend
# host at the browser's resolver, so a test cannot reach it whatever the config
# says. That is a guarantee; "the config is absent" was only a circumstance.
#
# Committed for the same reason .env.production is: both values are compiled
# into the public bundle, so the publishable key is an identifier and RLS is the
# access control. The sb_secret_ key appears nowhere.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://ohbzjwbcycbvjljffpcw.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_bW-3Vm8qgi4za6s37x5R5A_TFwCJuK-
